This project builds on maintained third-party standards tooling rather than
claiming to independently implement every OpenAPI and JSON Schema dialect:
- @apidevtools/json-schema-ref-parser: JSON Reference graph transformations (MIT)
- OpenAPI Initiative schemas: version-specific document structure (Apache-2.0)
- ajv-draft-04: draft-04 schema evaluation (MIT)
- ajv: JSON Schema vocabulary/meta-schema checks (MIT)
- buffer: scoped browser compatibility for the reference engine (MIT)
- yaml: YAML 1.2 parsing, syntax trees and serialization (ISC)
- ipaddr.js: IP address classification (MIT)

The exact installed versions are pinned in package-lock.json. Installed package
license files are authoritative. Transitive dependencies retain their licenses.
Swagger Parser and Redocly are development-only comparison/validation tools, not
the public API engine. Full production dependency license texts are collected in
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt during the build.
